            <ArticleTitle>Emergency off-pump coronary artery bypass (OPCAB) for left main coronary occlusion using rapid aorto-coronary perfusion.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>495-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>64 year old female with occluded left main after first injection brought to the operating room in extremis on IABP and maximum inotropes. LAD grafted with sapenous vein and immediate aorto-coronary perfusion. Circumflex grafted and patient taken to ICU. Patient discharged on POD #6 after echo shows normal ventricular with no wall motion abnormality.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
